<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42616" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sarda</span></b> , ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A kind of fish</i> that was pickled or salted,
			perh. <i>sardine</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 32,
				11, 53, § 151</span></i>; <i><span class="en">32, 5, 17, §
			46</span></i>.—Also called sardina, <i><span class="en">Col. 8,
				17, 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A kind of precious stone</i>, perh. <i>carnelian</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37, 7, 31, §
			105</span></i>.&lt;</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
